herdr guide 4: config and upkeep
================================

After herdr-3-agents. Change keys and settings, and upgrade herdr.

WHERE CONFIG LIVES
  ~/.dotfiles/herdr/config.toml   Shared settings (this repo)
  ~/.config/herdr/config.local.toml
                                  Settings for this machine only (not in this repo)
  ~/.config/herdr/config.toml     Generated from the two files above. Do not edit
  herdr-config-sync               Write the generated file and reload the running server
  herdr --default-config          Print every setting and default key, with comments

CHANGE A KEY
  1. Find the action name in herdr --default-config, for example rename_pane =
     "prefix+shift+p".
  2. Add the line under [keys] in the shared or local file.
  3. Run herdr-config-sync.
  4. Check for clashes first: grep the default config for the new key.

CUSTOM COMMAND KEYS
  [[keys.command]]
  key = "prefix+alt+g"
  type = "popup"   # popup: modal terminal; pane: temporary pane; shell: runs in background
  command = "lazygit"
  width = "80%"
  height = "80%"

UPGRADE
  mise upgrade herdr              Install the new version
  herdr server stop               Restart the server on the new version (closes panes; a
                                  service manager starts it again)
  herdr status                    Check that client and server versions match and are
                                  compatible
  agents-sync                     Refresh the herdr skill for agents
  Upgrade the laptop too. herdr --remote needs matching protocols on both sides
